.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-AUTODEPLOY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-autodeploy
.Nd after first boot, bring up what the install asked for: Kubernetes, the lab's goldens, the local AI
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl -want
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa kldload-autodeploy.service
runs
.Nm
once, after
.Xr kldload-firstboot 8 .
It reads the install manifest for what was asked for and brings each part
up in this order:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
the local AI, in the background: the GPU, Ollama through
.Xr kldload-ollama-install 8 ,
and the models the image carries; a model that must be downloaded waits
for the next step to finish, since running both at once made first boot
restart itself;
.It
Kubernetes, by
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
until the cluster is Ready or fails;
.It
the lab's goldens, the longest, last;
.It
the AI model warmed once it is there.
.El
.Pp
Each part that finishes leaves a marker in
.Pa /var/lib/kldload ,
and
.Pa all-ready
when every part asked for has one; the web console's first-boot banner
reads them, and
.Pa current-phase
says what is running.
A part that fails is logged and does not stop the others.
Running it again skips what already has a marker.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -want
Print what this install asked for, as
.Ql k8s= Ns Ar n Li klab= Ns Ar n Li ai= Ns Ar n ,
and exit 0, doing none of it.
The first-boot screen asks it whether to wait.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_AUTODEPLOY_PARALLEL_AI
1 lets the model download run alongside the Kubernetes bootstrap.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/install-manifest.env
What the install asked for.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/
The markers:
.Pa ai-ready , k8s-ready , k8s-phase-done , klab-ready , all-ready ,
.Pa current-phase .
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/autodeploy.log
Every phase.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when it ran; each part's failure is in the log and in its missing
marker, not in the exit status.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop installed with Kubernetes, the lab and AI, on
2026-09-30, with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-autodeploy --want
k8s=1 klab=1 ai=1
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr kldload-firstboot 8 ,
.Xr kldload-ollama-install 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-06-15 a first boot with everything asked for restarted itself
over and over: the model download ran alongside the cluster and the golden
builds.
On 2026-09-13 it piped Ollama's installer into a shell on a machine meant
to be offline.
